{0 Portable filesystem delivery}

{!Observe_fs} owns daily UTC filename selection, compact NDJSON projection,
finite admission, FIFO delivery, flush barriers, failure, and shutdown. It
performs no concrete filesystem or scheduler operation.

Integration authors implement {!Observe_fs.IO.S} and apply
{!Observe_fs.Make}. The drain callback synchronously converts a completed log
into owned bytes before returning [Accepted]. The resulting worker can then
perform effects without retaining the consumer's OCaml value.

Most Lwt-Unix applications should use [Observe_fs_lwt_unix.create] from the
ready package instead.
